ADR Index — website-os (Terminal-OS / NEOS)

Scope: Phases 0 → 3
Purpose: Single entry point for architectural decisions, constraints, and future intent.

⸻

Phase 0 — Foundations

ADR-0001 — Project Structure & Tech Stack

Summary
	•	React 18 + Vite + TypeScript
	•	SCSS modules with theme tokens
	•	OS metaphor (shell, apps, services)

Notes
	•	All later ADRs assume this stack.
	•	No framework churn without a new ADR.

⸻

Phase 1 — Engine & Determinism

ADR-0010 — Deterministic Engines & Testability

Summary
	•	Arcade engines must be deterministic.
	•	Fixed timesteps, seeded randomness where applicable.

Downstream impact
	•	Establishes the expectation that stateful systems must be testable.
	•	Influences VFS testing in Phase 3.

⸻

Phase 2 — Shell, Windowing, and Stability

ADR-0020 — Shell / App / Service Separation

Summary
	•	Shell manages windows and layout.
	•	Apps render content only.
	•	Services own state and persistence.

Downstream impact
	•	VFS introduced in Phase 3 must live as a service.
	•	FileMan.EXE consumes VFS; never owns it.

⸻

ADR-0021 — Desktop Layering Model

Summary
	•	HomeDashboard renders inside WindowManager, beneath windows.
	•	Fixes provider/layering errors.

Downstream impact
	•	FileMan.EXE must not assume it owns the desktop.
	•	All system apps behave as windows.

⸻

ADR-0022 — Mobile Terminal Independence

Summary
	•	Terminal.EXE on mobile is full-height.
	•	Not dependent on WindowManager.

Downstream impact
	•	System apps must tolerate multiple shell contexts.
	•	FileMan.EXE cannot rely on desktop-only affordances.

⸻

ADR-0023 — DOM Guards & Defensive Rendering

Summary
	•	Guard all DOM access.
	•	No assumptions about environment presence.

Downstream impact
	•	Phase 3 persistence and reset must not cause lifecycle crashes.

⸻

Phase 3 — File System, Persistence, Hardening

ADR-0030 — VFS Persistence & Schema Versioning

Summary
	•	Introduces persistent VFS service.
	•	localStorage-backed, versioned schema.
	•	Deterministic seed overlay.

Status
	•	Accepted for Phase 3 only.

⸻

ADR-0031 — Reset Semantics

Summary
	•	Reset is destructive and first-class.
	•	Always restores seeded state.
	•	Requires explicit confirmation.

⸻

ADR-0032 — FileMan.EXE Action Model

Summary
	•	Create / rename / delete / reset.
	•	Inline rename, keyboard-friendly.
	•	FileMan is the reference VFS consumer.

⸻

ADR-0033 — Testing Boundaries for Stateful Services

Summary
	•	VFS: unit tests only.
	•	FileMan: integration tests.
	•	No snapshot or E2E testing.

⸻

ADR-0034 — Live Embedded ME.OS Instance

Summary
	•	`ME.EXE` and fullscreen `ME.OS` are the same running instance.
	•	Desktop panel displays a live miniature of `ME.OS`.
	•	Fullscreen expands/collapses without resetting `ME.OS` state.

Downstream impact
	•	Requires shared state container for panel/fullscreen rendering modes.
	•	Prevents duplicate instances with divergent state.
	•	Needs mode-aware performance profile for panel rendering.

⸻

ADR-0035 — Context-Aware Global Menu

Summary
	•	One global Start-like menu button in bottom status bar.
	•	Menu entries adapt to active scope (Desktop, `ME.OS`, other subsystem scopes).
	•	Core menu component remains shared across scopes.

Downstream impact
	•	Prevents fragmented menu implementations.
	•	Supports subsystem-specific actions without changing global layout.
	•	Maintains consistent keyboard and accessibility behavior.

⸻

⚠️ Forward-Looking Intent (Important)

ADR-0090 — File System Evolution (Intent Record)

Status: Intentional / Not Implemented
Phase: Post-Phase 3 (future)

Statement of intent

The current Phase 3 VFS design is not final.
The file system model is expected to change in a future phase.

Reasons (non-exhaustive)
	•	Possible move away from simple tree storage
	•	Potential support for:
	•	richer metadata
	•	alternative backends
	•	virtual mounts
	•	app-scoped storage
	•	Desire to avoid over-engineering the Phase 3 VFS

Constraints
	•	Phase 3 decisions must:
	•	be replaceable
	•	avoid leaking VFS internals into apps
	•	keep migration paths possible

Rule
	•	No later ADR may assume the Phase 3 VFS structure is permanent.
	•	Any future redesign must reference this intent ADR.

⸻

ADR-0091 — Subsystem Parity Expansion (Intent Record)

Status: Intentional / Not Implemented
Phase: Post-Phase 3 (future)

Summary
	•	Non-ME panels (`YOU`, `THIRD`, `CONNECT`) are intended to adopt the same live panel + fullscreen shared-instance model used by `ME.OS`.
	•	Each subsystem should preserve state between panel and fullscreen modes.
	•	Mode-aware performance remains required for panel previews.

Additional intent
	•	`YOU`: forum/message-board direction with moderation constraints.
	•	`THIRD`: interactive 3D dimension with panel-mode pause/throttle behavior.
	•	`CONNECT`: game-hub direction, including future multiplayer support.

Reference
	•	`docs/subsystem-expansion-roadmap.md`

